            <ArticleTitle>[Anti-inflammatory and analgesic effects of scolopendra from different habitats].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>498-9, 512</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The water extracts of several species of the Chinese drug scolopendra from different habitats can inhibit obviously the increased permeability of abdominal blood capillaries and ear inflammation in mice. They can also raise the pain thresholds in mice during hot-plate and writhing tests. Their toxicity is very low.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
